Hi Statnet List,

I heard there had been a suggestion passed your way awhile back for a 
few feature requests, including a "Force MCMC" parameter and the ability 
to extract objects from the summary.ergm command (i.e. summary.ergm can 
return objects from the output it prints).  By a "Force MCMC" parameter 
I mean a feature that can force ergm to use the MCMC, even if the model 
has no dependence terms, so that I can use the proposal constraints.  
Additionally, I've noticed a bug where I cannot extracting the AIC 
through ergm.object$aic when I use the triangle parameter.

Has there been any improvements or modifications to these features?  I 
understand all contribution to statnet is entirely voluntary so any help 
on these matters would be greatly appreciated.

Thanks for putting together such a useful package.

-Ben

From handcock at stat.washington.edu  Sat Mar  3 12:55:26 2007
From: handcock at stat.washington.edu (Mark S. Handcock)
Date: Sat Mar  3 12:55:26 2007
Subject: [statnet_help] Feature Request
In-Reply-To: <45DF4BC7.8080701@uci.edu>
Message-ID: <C20F20BE.C872%handcock@stat.washington.edu>

Hi Ben,

Thanks for the suggestions. We are in the process of adding a lot of
features in preparation for the Workshop at this year's Sunbelt Conference
in Corfu (http://nicomedia.math.upatras.gr/conf/Sunbelt2007).

These are good ideas and we have updated "statnet" to version 1.0-14 to
accommodate them. Explicitly:

1) To force the use of the MCMC algorithm for dyad independence models, give
the option "force.mcmc" e.g.,

fit <- ergm(flomarriage ~ edges, algorithm.control=list(force.mcmc=T))

2) There is a new summary command called "Summary.ergm" that returns all the
objects it prints. For example,

# The usual summary
Summary.ergm(fit)
# Save the results
out <- Summary.ergm(fit)
names(out)
out$aic
out$asycov

out

This will be made the default is an upcoming version.

To get the new version, as usual, enter:

library(updatestatnet)

Mark

