Hi Ales.

How would you propose to set these parameters if you could?  The low 
probability of cross-sex ties can come from more than one underlying 
process.  For example, if there is a moderate assortative bias, a triad 
closure operating on top of this could result in even fewer cross-sex 
ties.  The outcome is thus a function of both underlying processes.  So 
which parameter would you fix?  And by how much?

best,
Martina

