Hello Martina.

My wish to set these parameters comes from being used to SIENA- Tom 
Snijders suggests fixing parameters that are hard to estimate, 
especially in cases where they have very strong effect. Especially in 
estimation procedures where the number of edges is kept fixed, the exact 
number to which the parameter should be set does not have to be 
specified very precisely.  E.g., in cases, where there are no ties 
between  boy and girls, any sufficiently high value will do. If the 
effect is not so "absolute", a bit more tweaking is needed, but from my 
experience with SIENA the appropriate number can be found in a few 
tries. You know that you have set/fixed the parameter to the appropriate 
number if the corresponding statistics in simulations on average matches 
the statistics in the data (and the variation is not to large).

Best,
Ales

