In-Reply-To: <47108AE2.4070102@gmail.com>
References: <47108AE2.4070102@gmail.com>
Message-ID: <Pine.WNT.4.64.0710190905570.6100@vinaya.csde.washington.edu>


Hello Ales (and all others interested in directed networks - please read 
on - there's a poll at the end):

The current release of statnet does not have directed versions of gwd, 
gwdsp, or gwesp in it.  However, we recognize the impotance of these and 
would be willing to code up some version of them for the new release of 
statnet to come out in the next few months.

One problem is that there are multiple different ways that each of these 
could be defined for directed networks. For instance, for gwdsp, one is 
counting multiple two-paths between two actors - we might code one 
statistic that counted any paths, regardless of direction, and others 
limiting to both ties out to the third actor, both ties in from the third 
actor, or the ties mixed.  Once you start counting combinations of these 
it can get even hairier.

So, we will be happy to code up some basic versions of gwd, gwdsp and 
gwesp for directed networks for the next statnet release, but will 
definitely need the help of the users to expand upon that set to include 
all versions of these statistics of interest. So this leads me to the 
poll.

Statnet Users: If you could have one definition for each of these three 
statistics for directed networks, what would it be? Would it consider all 
ties equally regardless of direction?  Or do something else? If there is a 
clear focus of interest around some definition, that will obviously be the 
version we choose to code up.

Cheers all,
Steve





