hello,

i also vote for the transitivity version of GWESP- this seems to me the 
only kind that is theoretically meaningful. it is a tough call for GWD, 
perhaps warranting both in- and out-, but if i had to choose i would go 
with out-ties only. finally, i also prefer the GWDSP term with two-paths 
going in the same direction (this term should tend to be negative, no? 
because it represents the "forbidden triad").

in general, then, i would like to see the distinction kept with 
directionality of ties. if, in particular instances, a researcher is 
justified in ignoring directionality for these terms, then i don't see 
why directionality should matter for other terms, and the network should 
just be symmetrized and analyzed with the current non-directed stats.

this is all very exciting though, and i'm looking forward to the new 
version!

-kevin

