From goodreau at u.washington.edu  Fri Oct 19 10:31:42 2007
From: goodreau at u.washington.edu (Steven Goodreau)
Date: Fri Oct 19 10:31:42 2007
Subject: [statnet_help] Fixing parameters
Message-ID: <Pine.WNT.4.64.0710191023200.6100@vinaya.csde.washington.edu>


Hi Ales,

This is another feature that's not in the current version of statnet, but 
which, it turns out, has already been coded up for the new release of 
statnet coming out in a few months.  You will be able to invoke it using 
the notation offset(statistic.to.fix). For example:

fit <- ergm(flomarriage ~ offset(edges) + kstar(2), theta0=c(-2,0.1))

will fix the edges coefficient to be -2 and estimates the kstar2 
coefficient as the MLE starting at an initial value of 0.1. Any terms or 
set of terms can be offset in this way.

Cheers,
Steve



