Ales,

I understand the purpose, but I would still be concerned that fixing one 
parameter would affect the estimates of other correlated parameters.  You 
might be able to match the corresponding model statistics, but the model 
would be wrong.

Fitting an offset does make sense if you have a good theoretical reason. 
Using an offset to solve an estimation problem should be done with care.

best,
mm

